Relates to #21412. Supersedes closed #21822 and #21664 once this consolidated branch is independently reviewed.

## Summary

This consolidates the browser-bridge workspace and the Chrome, Firefox, and Safari packaging/store contracts while retaining the security hardening that previously existed only on #21664:

- execution-time action authorization with fresh settings, session identity, effective host grant, policy, pause/control, incognito, and current-site checks;
- strict auto-pair Origin policy (known extension origins or originless loopback only);
- browser/API/companion response binding and filtered tab metadata;
- durable running-session resume and idempotent content recovery;
- no broad all-frame wallet-shim injection;
- Safari smoke executes instead of being a Node `import.meta.main` no-op.

Independent review added three exact-head corrections:

- relay success bodies are now structurally validated and bound to the paired companion/browser/profile before any session is accepted;
- content-script capture and action requests are bound to the exact URL authorized by the background worker, closing a navigation TOCTOU window;
- the Chromium smoke now performs a real DOM click through the built extension and verifies progress/completion callbacks, rather than stopping after sync.

## Exact-head evidence

<!-- evidence-head:07dffb04949d85b7e582b24e569ee172731344d0 -->

Pinned Bun 1.3.14 / Node 24.15.0:

- PASS: extension unit suite, 10 files / 53 tests;
- PASS: extension and `plugin-browser` typechecks;
- PASS: origin-policy packaging tests, 2 files / 8 tests;
- PASS: personal-assistant browser-session claim tests, 2/2;
- PASS: real built extension + Chromium pairing, sync, DOM click, progress, and completion smoke;
- PASS: Chrome and Firefox builds and reproducible Firefox package smoke, SHA-256 `2d932c9961ae2ad2c6d3ca5a618995fcef042ff11f5910c65a51851159293015`;
- PASS: Biome on all 43 extension files, guide parity, and `git diff --check`;
- FAIL: the exact-head Safari smoke built the Safari web extension but Safari did not register the temporary extension after the install step;
- FAIL: `bun run verify` reached 289/358 successful tasks, then stopped on pre-existing-surface UI test type errors outside this PR's diff (`BuildBadge-timeout.test.ts` and `load-pack-timeout.test.ts` import symbols not exported by their owning modules).

## Evidence Gate

- Before screenshots: N/A — restoration of a missing workspace.
- After screenshots/video/OCR: pending exact-head Chrome, Firefox, and Safari manager/popup captures and the required walkthrough.
- Backend/frontend logs: deterministic Chromium action smoke reviewed locally; immutable inline logs remain pending. Firefox and Safari installed-browser logs remain pending.
- LLM trajectory: N/A — no model behavior.
- Domain artifacts: Chrome/Firefox builds and Firefox repeat-hash proof passed locally. Immutable exact-head artifacts are not attached. Safari app/project archive repeat-hash proof is also pending.

## Merge blockers

1. Load the exact-head XPI in the currently supported Firefox and prove pair, sync, and one action; the repository's Firefox smoke currently proves build/package/repeatability only.
2. Resolve Safari temporary-extension registration without bypassing host safeguards, then prove exact-head install, pair, sync, and one action on Safari.
3. Attach the issue/CONTRIBUTING evidence matrix: browser manager/popup screenshots, walkthrough video, relevant logs, and immutable exact-head artifacts/checksums.
4. Add repeat-hash evidence for the Safari app/project archive on the available Xcode toolchain.
5. Restore a green exact-head root `bun run verify` (or land/rebase the upstream UI repair and rerun it).

## Contribution provenance

